    description:
      "Ameripolish is a name recognized throughout the polished concrete industry, and its LS/CS lithium densifier is the same professional-grade formula that flooring contractors specify for commercial polished floors in retail stores, warehouses, and showrooms. We include it here specifically for homeowners and builders dealing with a newly poured interior slab — a fresh basement floor or a new garage addition — because the densification chemistry works best on concrete that has not yet been contaminated by curing compounds, sealers, or years of tracked-in dirt and oil. On a 28-day-cured basement slab in a new home construction test, we applied Ameripolish LS/CS according to spec: flood coat, keep wet for 20 minutes with a light water misting, then squeegee and dry-mop the excess. Compared against Ghostshield's consumer densifier applied to an identical adjacent section, penetration depth testing using a simple cut-and-inspect method showed the Ameripolish product penetrating measurably deeper into the pore structure, which the manufacturer attributes to a smaller lithium silicate molecule size and a proprietary carrier system developed for professional polishing applications. This deeper penetration translates to a harder, more uniform wear surface across the full treated depth, not just the top few millimeters. For homeowners planning to have a basement or garage slab professionally polished down the road, treating with Ameripolish LS/CS early — even years before the polishing project — gives the contractor a head start, since many will apply their own densifier as part of the polishing process regardless. For those not polishing, this product still functions as an excellent zero-maintenance base treatment, and it plays well with color hardeners and concrete dyes if you are planning a stained decorative floor, since it does not interfere with dye absorption the way some topical sealers can. Zero VOC content and no measurable odor make it entirely reasonable to apply in a basement that shares HVAC ductwork with living space above. The tradeoff is availability — this is a professional product typically sourced through concrete supply houses or online rather than picked up at a big box hardware store, and it works best as part of a planned project rather than a same-day impulse fix for a dusty floor.",
