            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How do I stop my concrete floor from dusting?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Concrete dusting happens when the surface layer of cement paste is soft, porous, or under-cured, and it wears away as fine dust. The fix is either a lithium silicate densifier, which chemically hardens the surface permanently, or a topical acrylic sealer, which fills surface pores and seals the dust in place. For the most complete and lasting dust elimination, apply a densifier first and a topical sealer on top.
            </p>
